<p>Use the following procedure to print on both sides of the paper.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, this function may not be available.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Set the same direction as that set in the application. 
 If not, printing will be performed without the correct binding position.</p></li>
<li><p>Depending on the printer you are using, it is 
 required that the duplex unit be installed.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used 
 Settings</span> tab or the <span class="Term-Soft">2 Sided/Layout/Booklet</span> 
 menu of the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Specify how you want to open the bound output 
 in the <span class="Term-Soft">2 sided:</span> list.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Click the <span class="Term-Soft">&lt;&lt; Collapse list</span> button if the <span class="Term-Soft">2 
 sided:</span> list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used Settings</span> 
 tab is not displayed.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="4">
<li><p>Specify <button aria-controls="dropdown-1" aria-expanded="false" class="help-dropdown-toggle" data-bs-target="#dropdown-1" data-bs-toggle="collapse" type="button">the binding margins</button> 
 as necessary.</p><div class="collapse help-dropdown" id="dropdown-1">
<ol>
<li><p>Open the <span class="Term-Soft">2 Sided/Layout/Booklet</span> 
 menu of the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab if the 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used Settings</span> tab is displayed.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Binding Margins...</span> 
 to open the <span class="Term-Soft">Binding Margins for 2 sided Printing</span> 
 dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Enter the respective widths of the front and back 
 binding margins.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
